      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{8}{4-x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{8}{4-x}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{8}{4-y}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{8}{4-y} \\\\ x(4-y) & =8 \\\\ 4x-xy & =8 \\\\ -xy & =8-4x \\\\ xy & =4x-8 \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x-8}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4x-8}{x}.\n$$",
